@verbs earmuffs tapones
@tier player
@title shutting out what you would rather not hear
@see say channels

Earmuffs are two things: a switch, and a list of what you stop
hearing while they are on. The verb is not translated yet.

  tapones            says how you are wearing them, and what is on
                     the list.
  tapones on         you put them on.
  tapones off        you take them off.

With them on you do not hear whatever is on the list. To work the
list:

  tapones <thing>         adds it if it was not there, removes it
                          if it was.
  tapones <thing> on      adds it.
  tapones <thing> off     removes it.
  tapones all             adds everything that can be shut out.
  tapones none            empties the list.

What you can shut out is what the bare verb tells you. Shouts are
first on that list, and the reason most people reach for this.

With your earmuffs on you cannot shout either: there is little
point calling out to somebody whose answer you will not hear.
